PART 2: GROCERY LIST APP OVERVIEW
================================================================================

WHAT IS THE GROCERY LIST APP?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The application lets users:

• Add grocery items

• Enter quantity

• Choose a category

• Enter a unit price

• View grocery items

• Mark items as purchased

• Edit existing items

• Delete items

• Filter items

• View summary statistics

• Track shopping progress

• Clear the list


================================================================================
CORE FEATURES
================================================================================

+----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| FEATURE              | PURPOSE                                       |
+----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
| Add Item             | Create a new grocery item                     |
| Quantity             | Track number required                         |
| Category             | Organize grocery items                        |
| Unit Price           | Store price per unit                          |
| Purchased            | Track whether item has been bought            |
| Edit                 | Modify an existing item                       |
| Delete               | Remove one item                              |
| Filter               | All / To Buy / Purchased                     |
| Total Cost           | quantity × price across items                 |
| Statistics           | Counts derived from items                    |
| Progress             | Percentage purchased                          |
| Clear All            | Remove all items                             |
+----------------------+-----------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
FEATURE SCOPE OF THIS DEMO
================================================================================

This implementation uses:

React State

for storing grocery items.


Therefore:

• Items remain available while the component is active

• State changes update the UI

• Items are NOT automatically persisted after a page reload


Persistence would be a separate feature using something such as:

• localStorage

• Backend API

• Database


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The supplied app does NOT perform API integration.

It is a client-side React state-management demo.


